     "n": 1,
     "text": "MISCELLANEOUS.",
     "end": "space"
    }
   ],
   "uncertain": false,
   "note": null
  },
  {
   "id": "r3",
   "type": "translated_stanza",
   "lines": [
    {
     "n": 1,
     "text": "1. The sun is covered by day with the same strip of",
     "end": "space"
    },
    {
     "n": 2,
     "text": "ambara ( sky ; cloth ) with which the moon is covered at",
     "end": "space"
    },
    {
     "n": 3,
     "text": "night: oh the misery of these !",
     "end": "space"
    }
   ],
   "uncertain": false,
   "note": null
  },
  {
   "id": "r4",
   "type": "translated_stanza",
   "lines": [
    {
     "n": 1,
     "text": "2. When self-restraint developed by discrimination be-",
     "end": "hyphen"
    },
    {
     "n": 2,
     "text": "comes manifest, and when the strong hold desire has upon",
     "end": "space"
    },
    {
     "n": 3,
     "text": "man is relaxed, there appears that perfection ( the last stage",
     "end": "space"
    },
    {
     "n": 4,
     "text": "of contemplation ) wherein even the lord of gods, becomes",
     "end": "space"
    },
    {
     "n": 5,
     "text": "an object of pity, wretched (as he is under the influence of",
     "end": "space"
    },
    {
     "n": 6,
     "text": "desire) on account of the strong distraction caused by the",
     "end": "space"
    },
    {
     "n": 7,
     "text": "enjoyment of greatness worn out of age.",
     "end": "space"
    }
   ],
   "uncertain": false,
   "note": null
  },
  {
   "id": "r5",
   "type": "translated_stanza",
   "lines": [
    {
     "n": 1,
     "text": "3. Learning formerly served to remove the pain (of",
     "end": "space"
    },
    {
     "n": 2,
     "text": "existence ) of those who possessed self-restraint. In course",
     "end": "space"
    },
    {
     "n": 3,
     "text": "of time it came to be used for securing sensual happiness",
     "end": "space"
    },
    {
     "n": 4,
     "text": "to sensualists. Seeing that the rulers of the earth are now",
     "end": "space"
    },
    {
     "n": 5,
     "text": "averse to learning, alas ! it is even going down and down",
     "end": "space"
    },
    {
     "n": 6,
     "text": "every day.",
     "end": "space"
    }
   ],
   "uncertain": false,
   "note": null
  },
  {
   "id": "r6",
   "type": "translated_stanza",
   "lines": [
    {
     "n": 1,
     "text": "4. The time (that was) happy on account of the enjoy-",
     "end": "hyphen"
    },
    {
     "n": 2,
     "text": "ment of lovely women is passed; and having, for long, wan-",
     "end": "hyphen"
    },
    {
     "n": 3,
     "text": "dered along this avenue of the world we are exhausted; now",
     "end": "space"
    },
    {
     "n": 4,
     "text": "( stationed ) on the bank of the Ganges (lit. the river of",
     "end": "space"
    },
    {
     "n": 5,
     "text": "heaven ) we send forth (lit. extend) with deep sighs ( the",
     "end": "space"
    },
    {
     "n": 6,
     "text": "cries of invocation with the words—S'iva, S'iva, S'iva.",
     "end": "space"
    },
    {
     "n": 7,
     "text": "",
     "end": "space"
    }
   ],
   "uncertain": false,
   "note": null
  },
  {
   "id": "r7",
   "type": "translated_stanza",
   "lines": [
    {
     "n": 1,
     "text": "5. Mahàdeva is the god, and the stream of the gods (the",
     "end": "space"
    },
    {
     "n": 2,
     "text": "Ganges ) alone is the stream (for me); caves are (my) abode,",
     "end": "space"
    },
    {
     "n": 3,
     "text": "and even the quarters ( my ) raiment; the Destroyer is ( to",
     "end": "space"
    },
    {
     "n": 4,
     "text": "me ) as a friend; and my vow—such conduct (as is ) free",
     "end": "space"
    },
    {
     "n": 5,
     "text": "from meanness; or why say more (on this subject), let me",
     "end": "space"
    },
    {
     "n": 6,
     "text": "be wedded to the Vata tree alone (lead a life of seclusion",
     "end": "space"
    },
    {
     "n": 7,
     "text": "and piety ).",
     "end": "space"
    }
   ],
   "uncertain": false,
   "note": null
  },
  {
   "id": "r8",
   "type": "translated_stanza",
   "lines": [
    {
     "n": 1,
     "text": "6. How very blessed, indeed, are some persons who, with",
     "end": "space"
    },
    {
     "n": 2,
     "text": "their shackles of worldly ties snapped and not looking out",
     "end": "space"
    },
    {
     "n": 3,
     "text": "for the irregular course of serpentine sensualism, pass, in the",
     "end": "space"
    }
   ],
   "uncertain": false,
   "note": null
  },
